  Cell["Optional settings", "Subsection"], Cell["For example: \
PlotSuperradiance[n,l,m,at,0.5,2,300,12000, \"RateTolerance\" -> 10^-5, \
\"MaxDepth\" -> 40000, \"Progress\" -> False]. Inspect $SRLastRun after a \
sweep and $SRLastSolve after an individual solve. Tighter tolerances may \
require a larger depth budget.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Validation on 9 November 2026", "Section"], 
  Cell["At 80-digit working precision, continued-fraction values agreed with \
the original to at least approximately 75 digits at five trial points, \
including l=7. Tests also checked continuation across unequal alpha gaps, \
option forwarding, three-point data export and the Gamma=2 Im[omega] \
convention. A small-alpha 211 point at spin 0.5, alpha 0.01 agreed with an \
80-digit, 40,000-term reference to about 1.5 x 10^-6 relatively in the rate."\
, "Text"], Cell["The timings below compare the original fixed-depth solver at \
Nmax=12000 with this copy's default adaptive solver, including its precision \
check. These are local single-solve measurements; full-sweep speed depends on \
level, alpha, spin, seeds and requested tolerance.", "Text"], 
  Cell["{2, 1, 1}  alpha=0.1  spin=0.5  original=4.96s  optimised=1.80s  rate \
relative difference=         -8\n3.13 \[Times] 10\n{2, 1, 1}  alpha=0.42  \
spin=0.99  original=7.62s  optimised=2.37s  rate relative difference=         \
-11\n6.52 \[Times] 10\n{3, 2, 2}  alpha=0.3  spin=0.99  original=6.00s  \
optimised=2.75s  rate relative difference=         -10\n3.95 \[Times] 10\n{4, \
2, 2}  alpha=0.3  spin=0.99  original=5.89s  optimised=3.06s  rate relative \
difference=         -9\n9.78 \[Times] 10\n{5, 4, 4}  alpha=1.2  spin=0.99  \
original=20.89s  optimised=11.13s  rate relative difference=         \
-14\n4.57 \[Times] 10", "Text"]}, WindowTitle -> 
